<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4543" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aurēlĭānus</span></b> ,
		i, m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Flavius Claudius, <i>a
				Roman emperor who reigned</i> A. D. 270-275; his life was
			written by Vopiscus; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
			489</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1026</span></i> sq.; 1535;
			1856.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aurēlĭānus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of Aurelian</i>:
			sodales, <i>a college of priests like the</i>
			Augustales, <i><span class="en">Capitol. M. Anton. Philos. 7 <i>fin.</i></span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">BALNEVM,</span>”
				<i>built by Aurelian</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Grut. 178, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aurēlĭānensis</span></b> ,
			e, adj.: urbs, the present <i>Orleans</i>, <i><span class="en">Sid. 8, 15</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
